# =============================================================================
# Dad Jokes API - Environment Variables (Example / Template)
# =============================================================================
# This file is a TEMPLATE for the real .env file. It shows what variables
# are needed without containing real secrets. New developers copy this file
# and fill in their own values.
#
# WHY does this file exist?
# - It's committed to Git (unlike .env) so everyone can see what vars are needed
# - It has safe placeholder values so nobody accidentally uses real credentials
# - It serves as documentation for what the app needs to run
# =============================================================================

# DB_HOST = The address of the computer where PostgreSQL (our database) is running.
# "localhost" means it's on YOUR computer. If the database were on a server
# in the cloud, you'd put that server's address here instead.
DB_HOST=localhost

# DB_PORT = The "door number" that PostgreSQL listens on.
# 5432 is PostgreSQL's default port (like how websites use port 80).
# Only change this if you configured PostgreSQL to use a different port.
DB_PORT=5432

# DB_USER = The username used to log into PostgreSQL.
# "postgres" is the default admin username that comes with PostgreSQL.
# You should change this to your own database username.
DB_USER=postgres

# DB_PASSWORD = The password for the database user above.
# "postgres" is the default password (very insecure — only use for local dev!).
# NEVER put a real production password here or commit it to Git.
DB_PASSWORD=postgres

# DB_NAME = The name of the specific database within PostgreSQL.
# PostgreSQL can hold many databases. This tells our app which one to use.
# You need to create this database before running the app (or it gets
# created automatically depending on your setup).
DB_NAME=dad_jokes

# PORT = The port our Express API server will run on.
# When you visit http://localhost:3001, you're hitting this server.
# This should match what's configured in vite.config.ts's proxy setting,
# so the frontend knows where to forward API requests.
PORT=3001
